getting a new phone is really exciting  and getting money for your old one is  two but before you send those devices  off to resell services like declutter or  gazelle or before you take it to your  mobile carrier to trade in there's a few  things you might want to do first  you want to be sure you're not handing  over a device with your personal data on  it or sending in a phone that's still  linked to your account so today we're  going to go through some of the best  ways to clean up your phone's hardware  and software so you'll be ready to part  ways with it  [Music]  okay so step one the first thing you  want to do is back up your phone's data  to a cloud or to a computer both are  pretty easy to do on iphones and  androids for your apple device go to  icloud settings and turn on icloud  backup  when your phone is connected to wi-fi  plugged in to charge and locked apple  will start adding your data to the cloud  you can also perform a manual backup by  tapping backup now  what's really annoying though is if your  icloud backup requires more than five  gigabytes of data you have to either  decide what content you don't want or  buy more storage  for updated android devices you can use  the backup by google one feature  launched in 2021 it gives you 15 gigs of  storage to back up your device or you  can pay for more if you want  one way you can try to get around  storage limits is to connect your phone  to a computer and back it up that way  either way be sure to backup your  phone's contacts photos videos really  anything that you would regret losing if  it's gone because once it's not saved  you probably won't get it back  it's also really smart to set up  automatic backups on your new device in  case you break it or happen to lose it  so now you're backed up  the next big thing you're going to want  to do is to sign out of all your  accounts you're going to want to go  through each of your apps and manually  sign out of your accounts that way those  services don't list old devices that  you've long since gotten rid of if  you're switching from iphone to android  be sure to sign out of imessages that  way you don't have any issues getting  new messages on your new device  now it's time to sign out of the phone  itself scroll to the bottom of your  apple id menu and tap sign out otherwise  the device will appear stolen and  there's nothing new owners can do with  it  and if you have an android you'll want  to go into your settings and log out of  your google account  [Music]  now you want to clear your data from the  phone and restore it so that all that  remains are whatever settings were  pre-installed by the manufacturer that's  where a factory reset comes in the exact  location of factory reset options varies  from phone to phone updated iphones  should give you a setting to transfer or  reset the phone under your general  settings  and here's what it looks like on an  android phone i had to poke around a  little bit but found it under the  general management settings  once the resets are done your phone  should be in its original state and  we're almost ready to go  [Music]  the final step is something you really  don't want to forget because it's a  little important clean the outside of  your phone making the phone look brand  new might help you get more money if  you're selling it online and it's also  just good hygiene  a good microfiber cloth an alcohol based  cleaner and a q-tip should do the trick  and with that the device you've been  carrying around is ready for its next  phase of life  with a new owner  i'll miss you  if you want to know more about the  latest tech and how it all works be sure  to subscribe to my channel and comment  below to let me know what i should look  into next until next time
 

